{"vid":"djZpQCzvTyI","source":"djZpQCzvTyI.en-orig.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.2,"txt":"MIG welding vertical joints can be one"},{"t":1.9,"txt":"of the most frustrating skills to learn,"},{"t":4,"txt":"but it doesn't have to be that bad, and"},{"t":5.7,"txt":"I'm going to walk you through it in this"},{"t":7.2,"txt":"video. Hey, welcome to the shop. Today,"},{"t":9.8,"txt":"we're going to go over vertical MIG,"},{"t":11.8,"txt":"both uphill and downhill. We'll talk"},{"t":13.6,"txt":"about how to keep your material from"},{"t":15.4,"txt":"piling up and go over some practical"},{"t":17.6,"txt":"tips and techniques. Now, let's start"},{"t":20.2,"txt":"off by talking about when you should go"},{"t":22.4,"txt":"uphill versus downhill. And this is a"},{"t":25.3,"txt":"huge debate and I'd love to know what"},{"t":27.2,"txt":"you think in the comments, but please"},{"t":28.8,"txt":"keep it respectful. While there are a"},{"t":30.5,"txt":"lot of nuances and you should definitely"},{"t":32.1,"txt":"make sure the technique you're using"},{"t":33.6,"txt":"works for your application, I use a"},{"t":36,"txt":"simple rule of thumb and that is just"},{"t":38.3,"txt":"the material thickness. 1/8 in thick"},{"t":41.5,"txt":"material can run vertical up or down. If"},{"t":44.2,"txt":"it's thinner than that, I'll usually run"},{"t":45.9,"txt":"it downhill. If it's thicker than that,"},{"t":47.6,"txt":"I'll usually run it uphill. We're going"},{"t":49,"txt":"to use 1/8 inch thick today. and we'll"},{"t":51.8,"txt":"run both downhill and uphill and look at"},{"t":54.3,"txt":"some of the differences. So, as far as"},{"t":56.4,"txt":"machine settings, most machine uh door"},{"t":58.9,"txt":"charts or the built-in settings for"},{"t":60.5,"txt":"synergic machines are based on running"},{"t":62.8,"txt":"in the flat and horizontal position, and"},{"t":65,"txt":"they're usually pretty good for downhill"},{"t":67.1,"txt":"MIG as well. So, here in my technique, I"},{"t":70.7,"txt":"need to pay attention to my stickout, my"},{"t":74,"txt":"work and travel angle, as well as my"},{"t":75.8,"txt":"travel speed. And notice I'm moving"},{"t":77.8,"txt":"pretty fast here to stay up ahead of"},{"t":80.2,"txt":"that weld puddle. I'm putting in"},{"t":82.2,"txt":"material and heat the whole time. And"},{"t":84.3,"txt":"I've got to stay up ahead of it to get"},{"t":86.1,"txt":"good penetration when I'm running"},{"t":87.5,"txt":"downhill. And that's why it's really"},{"t":89.2,"txt":"best for thinner material. I'm not using"},{"t":91.4,"txt":"much travel angle. I'm just slightly"},{"t":93.8,"txt":"above perpendicular to the plate. And"},{"t":96.5,"txt":"this is a really easy technique and"},{"t":98.5,"txt":"doesn't require a whole lot more than"},{"t":100.1,"txt":"running in the flat and horizontal"},{"t":101.4,"txt":"position. and gives really good results"},{"t":103.1,"txt":"when you're on thinner material. 1/8"},{"t":105.2,"txt":"inch thick and thinner is kind of my"},{"t":107,"txt":"rule of thumb again. And it can uh be"},{"t":110.3,"txt":"really strong here and holds up really"},{"t":112.6,"txt":"well. Definitely outruns the base metal."},{"t":114.6,"txt":"You can see the back of that plate"},{"t":116.6,"txt":"didn't open up at all. So, it's my"},{"t":118.9,"txt":"preferred method for thin material. That"},{"t":120.7,"txt":"joint turned out great and I've had"},{"t":122.2,"txt":"really good results running downhill on"},{"t":124.5,"txt":"1/8 inch thick material. And as you get"},{"t":126.2,"txt":"into thinner sheet metal, um it works"},{"t":128.8,"txt":"really, really well. Now, let's try"},{"t":131.4,"txt":"running vertical up with that exact same"},{"t":134.1,"txt":"technique and those settings and see"},{"t":136,"txt":"what happens. Now, with vertical up, I'm"},{"t":138.6,"txt":"putting metal and heat in at the same"},{"t":140.4,"txt":"rate that I was before, but notice how"},{"t":142.4,"txt":"slow I'm traveling to stay with that"},{"t":144.4,"txt":"weld puddle because I'm fighting gravity"},{"t":146.4,"txt":"as I try to move my way up. And this is"},{"t":149.5,"txt":"really the issue. So, all that heat and"},{"t":151.4,"txt":"metal has to go somewhere and it"},{"t":153.5,"txt":"typically droops out and piles up below."},{"t":156.9,"txt":"And if you run this way, you're going to"},{"t":159,"txt":"end up with a big crown on your weld."},{"t":162.1,"txt":"Now, there are some advantages to that"},{"t":163.9,"txt":"because you have so much time for that"},{"t":165.7,"txt":"heat to soak in that you can really"},{"t":168.2,"txt":"penetrate on thicker material, but that"},{"t":170.4,"txt":"crown on the weld bead profile is less"},{"t":172.2,"txt":"than ideal. Now, this is still a pretty"},{"t":174.7,"txt":"strong weld, and I've certainly bought"},{"t":176.1,"txt":"products with worse welds than that, but"},{"t":178.2,"txt":"we can do better by making two changes"},{"t":180.2,"txt":"to our settings and our technique. I'm"},{"t":182.9,"txt":"going to reduce my wire feed speed. And"},{"t":184.9,"txt":"I found a good rule of thumb is drop it"},{"t":187.1,"txt":"by right around 30%. And that uh gets"},{"t":191.3,"txt":"you in the ballpark without putting too"},{"t":192.9,"txt":"much wire in as you wait for that puddle"},{"t":194.6,"txt":"to rise. But the default voltage for"},{"t":197.1,"txt":"that wire feed is probably going to be a"},{"t":198.9,"txt":"bit low. So I turned that up about a"},{"t":200.4,"txt":"volt and a half. Now the way we're going"},{"t":202.1,"txt":"to change the technique is introduce a"},{"t":204.3,"txt":"slight weave. Now I'm not weaving"},{"t":206.2,"txt":"outside of the puddle like some people"},{"t":208,"txt":"do to stack dimes. I'm sticking with a"},{"t":210.5,"txt":"weld puddle. Imagine it about this wide."},{"t":213.3,"txt":"And I'm just moving from side to side."},{"t":216.1,"txt":"Quick through the middle and slow on the"},{"t":218,"txt":"edges. Quick through the middle and slow"},{"t":219.4,"txt":"on the edges. And notice there's a"},{"t":220.7,"txt":"little bit of an arc to it just to touch"},{"t":223.3,"txt":"the front uh leading edge and advance"},{"t":225.6,"txt":"things a little bit as I work my way up."},{"t":227.9,"txt":"The overall travel speed is about the"},{"t":229.9,"txt":"same that I had before, except now I'm"},{"t":231.9,"txt":"putting in 30% less wire. And I'm using"},{"t":234.9,"txt":"that slight weave just to spread that"},{"t":237.3,"txt":"weld out and smooth it over a little bit"},{"t":239.5,"txt":"to tie into the corners without having"},{"t":241.7,"txt":"so much uh just up as a crown on top. So"},{"t":245.4,"txt":"notice I'm getting a little bit of"},{"t":247,"txt":"spatter. I might have gone just a little"},{"t":248.3,"txt":"bit high on the voltage, but it's"},{"t":250.2,"txt":"definitely workable. Now, the exact"},{"t":252.2,"txt":"pattern that you use isn't all that"},{"t":254.1,"txt":"important. You could do more of a zigzag"},{"t":256,"txt":"or triangle, and it's going to work just"},{"t":258.1,"txt":"fine uh either way. The principle is"},{"t":260.7,"txt":"you're just spreading this out. Now,"},{"t":262.4,"txt":"notice I don't put my wire clear to the"},{"t":264.2,"txt":"edge of the puddle. There's a bit of a"},{"t":266.6,"txt":"diameter around it. So, I'm just"},{"t":268.2,"txt":"watching the edge of that puddle and"},{"t":269.7,"txt":"trying to keep it as even as possible."},{"t":271.8,"txt":"You can see that it did heat soak a"},{"t":273.6,"txt":"little bit up towards the top. So, it"},{"t":274.9,"txt":"was a little more challenging to keep"},{"t":276.3,"txt":"that weld spread out with this uh 1/8"},{"t":279,"txt":"inch thick on these smaller coupons."},{"t":280.9,"txt":"That's not as big of a problem on a"},{"t":282.7,"txt":"larger project with more mass or on"},{"t":284.6,"txt":"thicker material, but it is something"},{"t":286.6,"txt":"that you end up dealing with when you're"},{"t":288.5,"txt":"running vertical up. Either way, the"},{"t":290.8,"txt":"weld is definitely strong and you got a"},{"t":293.1,"txt":"lot of heat into it and there's no"},{"t":294.7,"txt":"separation there at the back side of the"},{"t":297.3,"txt":"joint. Now, if we take a look at the"},{"t":299.4,"txt":"bottom, you can see with this downhill"},{"t":302.1,"txt":"how much less heat soak there is as I"},{"t":304.8,"txt":"worked through than when I was running"},{"t":306.6,"txt":"uphill. When I ran uphill, it heat"},{"t":308.5,"txt":"soaked that whole side and the top"},{"t":310.6,"txt":"there. So, you definitely have a lot"},{"t":312.2,"txt":"more heat input that's going to affect"},{"t":313.5,"txt":"distortion and things like that. Um, so"},{"t":315.8,"txt":"there are pros and cons. Thanks for"},{"t":318.1,"txt":"tuning in today. Hey, if you enjoyed"},{"t":319.4,"txt":"this or learned something, let me know"},{"t":320.6,"txt":"by hitting that thumbs up below or"},{"t":322.1,"txt":"leaving me a comment. And if you are"},{"t":324.2,"txt":"looking to level up your skills and you"},{"t":325.8,"txt":"want me to walk through the whole"},{"t":327,"txt":"learning process with you in small baby"},{"t":329.5,"txt":"steps that make it so much easier to"},{"t":331.5,"txt":"learn, check out my affordable online"},{"t":333.3,"txt":"courses linked in the description. We'll"},{"t":335,"txt":"see you next time."}],"words":[{"t":0.16,"w":"MIG"},{"t":0.48,"w":"welding"},{"t":0.8,"w":"vertical"},{"t":1.199,"w":"joints"},{"t":1.52,"w":"can"},{"t":1.68,"w":"be"},{"t":1.839,"w":"one"},{"t":1.92,"w":"of"},{"t":2,"w":"the"},{"t":2.159,"w":"most"},{"t":2.399,"w":"frustrating"},{"t":2.96,"w":"skills"},{"t":3.28,"w":"to"},{"t":3.52,"w":"learn,"},{"t":4,"w":"but"},{"t":4.16,"w":"it"},{"t":4.4,"w":"doesn't"},{"t":4.56,"w":"have"},{"t":4.72,"w":"to"},{"t":4.799,"w":"be"},{"t":4.96,"w":"that"},{"t":5.2,"w":"bad,"},{"t":5.52,"w":"and"},{"t":5.68,"w":"I'm"},{"t":5.92,"w":"going"},{"t":6,"w":"to"},{"t":6.08,"w":"walk"},{"t":6.24,"w":"you"},{"